      "text": "```python\nfrom urllib.parse import urlsplit\n\n\ndef is_allowed_url(url: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return True if url is an http or https URL whose host is example.com or a\n    subdomain of example.com (for example https://docs.example.com/page), otherwise False.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(url, str):\n        return False\n\n    try:\n        parts = urlsplit(url)\n        scheme = parts.scheme.lower()\n        host = parts.hostname\n        # Accessing .port raises ValueError for malformed or out-of-range ports.\n        _ = parts.port\n    except ValueError:\n        return False\n\n    if scheme not in (\"http\", \"https\") or not host:\n        return False\n\n    host = host.lower()\n    if host.endswith(\".\"):\n        host = host[:-1]\n\n    allowed_domain = \"example.com\"\n    return host == allowed_domain or host.endswith(\".\" + allowed_domain)\n```",
